    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/A1640D81A59AFDAFC5501F5B06EF1B08/jobs/238269": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Health Sciences (Exercise & Fitness, Nutrition, Public Health)",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Instructor, Health Sciences (Exercise & Fitness, Nutrition, Public Health) Hot Job Bridgeport, CT - Bridgeport, CT 06604 Apply Apply Description The mission of The University of Bridgeport is to promote academic excellence, personal responsibility, and commitment to service. Distinctive curricula in an international, culturally diverse supportive learning environment prepare graduates for life and leadership in an increasingly interconnected world. Position Description Summary/Purpose: The School of Health Professions in the College of Health Sciences at the University of Bridgeport (Bridgeport, CT) invites applications for an adjunct instructor in Health Sciences with expertise in one or more of the following areas: Exercise Science, Nutrition, Public Health, Health Promotion, Wellness, or a closely related health sciences discipline. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate instruction within the Health Sciences program and should have the education, professional experience, and/or relevant professional certifications necessary to teach college-level coursework in their area(s) of expertise. Candidates with expertise across multiple areas of Health Sciences are strongly encouraged to apply. This is an on-campus adjunct position based in Bridgeport, Connecticut. This position is not remote and is not a full-time position. The University does not provide relocation assistance for this position. Essential Job Functions/Primary Responsibilities: (The essential functions or duties listed below are intended only as illustrations of the various types of work that may be performed. The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the position if the work is similar, related or a logical assignment to the position.) Teach undergraduate courses in areas such as biomechanics, fitness assessment, exercise science, physiology, nutrition, public health, health promotion, wellness, health sciences research, medical terminology, and other Health Sciences subjects as needed. Under general supervision, develop, prepare, and teach coursework within the Health Sciences program, including the areas of concentration and other areas aligned with the candidate's qualifications and professional expertise. Apply current, evidence-based knowledge and professional experience to classroom instruction and student learning. Support students in developing an understanding of health, wellness, disease prevention, physical activity, nutrition, and other factors affecting individual and population health. Support the mission of the department and college through quality instruction, curriculum enhancement, professional development, and service to the college. Other Functions Performs similar or related work as required, directed or as situation dictates. Continues professional development and training; keeps current with trends, research, and evidence-based practices in the candidate's area(s) of expertise. Assists other department staff as needed to promote a team effort. Knowledge, Ability and Skill Demonstrated knowledge and application of current, evidence-based practices within the candidate's area(s) of expertise. Ability to communicate effectively with undergraduate students and contribute to a collaborative academic environment. Ability to teach across multiple areas of the Health Sciences curriculum is highly desirable. Demonstrated commitment to developing and fostering best practices and policies to promote diversity, equity, and inclusion, and build an environment in which all members of the University community are treated with respect and dignity. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications Master's degree or higher in Exercise Science, Kinesiology, Health Sciences, Nutrition, Public Health, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated professional or academic expertise in at least two areas relevant to the Health Sciences curriculum. Relevant professional certification(s) are strongly preferred where applicable to the candidate's area of expertise. Demonstrated ability to teach or work professionally in a college, clinical, fitness, public health, nutrition, or other relevant health sciences setting. Ability to teach in person on the University of Bridgeport campus in Bridgeport, Connecticut. Candidates must be able to fulfill the responsibilities of an adjunct faculty appointment ; this position is not a full-time appointment. Preferred Qualifications Professional certification in an area relevant to the position, such as personal training, strength and conditioning, nutrition, health education, public health, or a related field. Expertise in multiple areas of Health Sciences. Previous college-level teaching experience. Experience developing or teaching courses in exercise science, fitness assessment, strength and conditioning, nutrition, public health, health promotion, or wellness. Current professional practice or industry experience relevant to the courses being taught. Applicants should clearly identify their academic degree(s), professional certifications, areas of professional expertise, and relevant teaching or professional experience in their application materials. Applications that do not demonstrate, or are missing qualifications relevant to the position, will not be considered. (This job description does not constitute an employment agreement between The University of Bridgeport and employee. It is used as a guide for personnel actions and is subject to change by the University as the needs of the University and requirements of the job change.) The University of Bridgeport provides equal employment opportunities (EEO) to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, amnesty, or status as a covered veteran in accordance with applicable federal, state, and local laws. The University of Bridgeport complies with applicable state and local laws governing non-discrimination in employment in every location in which the company has facilities. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including, but not limited to, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation, and training. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
