      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Anatomy & Physiology",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Instructor - Anatomy & Physiology Hot Job Bridgeport, CT - Bridgeport, CT 06604 Apply Apply Description The mission of The University of Bridgeport is to promote academic excellence, personal responsibility, and commitment to service. Distinctive curricula in an international, culturally diverse supportive learning environment prepare graduates for life and leadership in an increasingly interconnected world. Position Description Summary/Purpose : The College of Science and Society at the University of Bridgeport seeks part-time Adjunct Faculty to teach undergraduate Anatomy and Physiology lecture and/or laboratory courses. Adjunct faculty report to the Department of Biology and work closely with the Associate Chair of Biology and the Lead Instructor to ensure consistency across sections. Courses follow a shared syllabus and shared exams, and all instructional materials are provided. Essential Job Functions/Primary Responsibilities : (The essential functions or duties listed below are intended only as illustrations of the various types of work that may be performed. The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the position if the work is similar, related or a logical assignment to the position.) Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Teach assigned Physiology/Anatomy and Physiology lecture and/or lab sections ( see below for course details and meeting times) Introductory Anatomy and Physiology I (BIOL-113): Lecture course, non-major Schedule: Tuesday/Thursday, 6:00 PM – 7:15 PM Intro Anatomy & Phys II Lab (BIOL-114L): Laboratory course, non-major Currently available sections: Tuesday 3:30 PM – 5:20 PM Tuesday 5:30 PM – 7:20 PM Tuesday 7:30 PM – 9:20 PM Additional sections may be offered. The incoming adjunct may teach one or more sections, depending on availability. General Physiology (BIOL-211): Lecture and laboratory course, biology majors Lecture: Tuesday/Thursday, 1:30 PM – 2:45 PM Lab: Thursday, 3:00 PM – 5:45 PM This course focuses on the physiological and biochemical regulation of body systems , with laboratory activities emphasizing experimentation and data interpretation. Implement courses as designed in approved syllabi Administer and grade shared quizzes, exams, and lab assessments Maintain attendance and academic records Upload grades to Canvas and University systems Communicate with students in a timely and professional manner Provide academic support via email and scheduled meetings as needed Meet all course and semester deadlines Start Date: January 12, 2026 Other Functions : Collaborate with the Associate Chair and Lead Instructor Participate in coordinated assessment and grading practices Perform related instructional duties as assigned Stay current within the field of Anatomy and Physiology Knowledge, Ability and Skill : Ability to teach effectively in in-person and/or online formats Familiarity with Canvas or similar learning management systems Strong organizational, communication, and time-management skills Commitment to high academic standards and student-centered teaching Ability to work collaboratively within a structured course framework Qualifications Minimum Required Qualifications : The successful candidate should have: Master’s degree in Biology, Anatomy & Physiology, or a related discipline Experience with undergraduate lab instruction Demonstrated ability to manage grading and course administration Applicants MUST submit a resume/CV AND a letter of interest (cover letter). Preferred Qualifications: PhD, MSN, DNP, PA, or DPT College-level A&P teaching experience Clinical or allied health professional experience (This job description does not constitute an employment agreement between The University of Bridgeport and employee. It is used as a guide for personnel actions and is subject to change by the employer as the needs of the employer and requirements of the job change.) Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
