    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/A1640D81A59AFDAFC5501F5B06EF1B08/jobs/293407": {
      "title": "Assistant Diving Coach (PT)",
      "description": "You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Diving Coach (PT) Hot Job Bridgeport, CT - Bridgeport, CT 06604 Apply Apply Description The mission of The University of Bridgeport is to promote academic excellence, personal responsibility, and commitment to service. Distinctive curricula in an international, culturally diverse supportive learning environment prepare graduates for life and leadership in an increasingly interconnected world. Position Description Summary/Purpose : The Part-Time Diving Coach assists the Head Men's and Women's Swimming & Diving Coach in all aspects of the University's NCAA Division II diving program. Responsibilities include coaching, student-athlete development, recruiting, and supporting a positive, competitive team culture while ensuring compliance with NCAA, conference, and University policies. Essential Job Functions/Primary Responsibilities : (The essential functions or duties listed below are intended only as illustrations of the various types of work that may be performed. The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the position if the work is similar, related or a logical assignment to the position.) Represent the University of Bridgeport and the Athletic Department in a positive manner with a high degree of integrity and quality. Promote and support the University of Bridgeport and its mission. Promote and support the University of Bridgeport Athletic Department’s program mission and goals. Adheres to and enforces all policies and procedures of the department and the University, as well as the rules and regulations of the NCAA, NE10 and any other authorities that affect the intercollegiate athletic program Coach and develop NCAA Division II divers in springboard 1M & 3M events through daily practices and competition. Design and implement training plans emphasizing technical skill development, safety, and performance improvement. Provide individualized instruction, video analysis, and meet preparation. Recruit and evaluate prospective student-athletes who align with the University's academic and athletic standards. Assist with travel, meet management, equipment maintenance, and other program operations. Foster academic success, sportsmanship, leadership, and personal development among student-athletes. Maintain compliance with all NCAA Division II, conference, and University rules and regulations. Collaborate with the Head Coach to support the overall success of the men's and women's swimming and diving program. Other Functions : Performs similar or related work as required, directed or as situation dictates. Continues professional development and training; keeps current with trends. Assists other department staff as needed to promote a team effort. Knowledge, Ability and Skill : Demonstrated commitment to developing and fostering best practices and policies to promote diversity, equity, and inclusion, and build an environment in which all members of the University community are treated with respect and dignity. Experience in collegiate diving Qualifications Minimum Required Qualifications : Education, Training and Experience : The qualifications required would generally be acquired with or any equivalent combination of education, work experience and training. Bachelor’s Degree or equivalent; advanced degree preferred; CPR/AED certification; College participation and/or coaching preferred Excellent verbal and written communication skills; Coaching and /or participation at collegiate level preferred; demonstrated ability and passion to teach and demonstrate skills in diving: Ability to work weekdays, evenings and weekends; Candidate must have a valid driver’s license and meet University of Bridgeport’s Driving Requirements ; Willingness to fundraise; Ability to interact with all levels of the university community. Special Requirements : Valid license & insured vehicle Physical and Mental Requirements 